     "text": "A lighting bulb on a home staircase is controlled by two switches: switch $S_1$ located at the ground floor and switch $S_2$ located at the first-floor landing. Changing the state of either switch reverses the state of the bulb (from ON to OFF, or from OFF to ON), regardless of the position of the other switch. The logical switching operation of this system resembles:  \n(A) AND Gate  \n(B) OR Gate  \n(C) XOR Gate  \n(D) NAND Gate"
